  "commit": "8b9ddbe999a34caf8fe091e7eefb58bc4e649055",
  "verdict": {
    "multiplicativity_holds_on_the_mean": true,
    "statement": "Every measured pair is ORTHOGONAL on the mean, with |I| at most 0.0952 log2 = a 6.8% error discrepancy. This is the FIRST time this campaign's stacking assumption has been measured rather than assumed, and it survives.",
    "but_not_per_cell": "No pair is orthogonal at EVERY cell. Worst cells reach I = +0.2851 (REDUNDANT, 1.218x the predicted error) and I = -0.1558 (SYNERGISTIC, 0.898x). So a stacked projection is sound in expectation and carries roughly a -10%/+22% per-cell band, which should be quoted with any stacked estimate rather than dropped.",
    "marginal_pair": "STRUCTURAL x ALGEBRAIC sits at 0.0952 against a 0.1 threshold -- inside the label by 5%. Calling it ORTHOGONAL is defensible only because the threshold was named before looking; it is the pair most likely to flip with more sites, and is flagged rather than presented as settled.",
    "unknowns_are_now_partly_answered": "DEPTH is UNKNOWN here for a stronger reason than when this obligation was written: G062 and G064 both refuted their mechanisms this session, so no live candidate varies depth at all. ENTROPY cannot move a functional error by construction -- the coding stage leaves dequantized values identical -- so it is not measurable on this harness and needs TOKEN_NS."
  }
